  "id": "13697_itametsukeru",
  "headword": "{痛|いた}めつける",
  "reading": "いためつける",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to torment, to beat up",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "ichidan",
    "stem": "{痛|いた}めつけ"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to torment, to beat up, to punish severely",
      "explanation": "To inflict repeated or severe physical or emotional pain on someone. Can refer to physical violence, harsh treatment, or causing great suffering."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "13697_itametsukeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{弱|よわ}い{者|もの}を{痛|いた}めつける。",
      "english": "To torment the weak.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13697_itametsukeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{相手|あいて}チームを{痛|いた}めつけて{大勝|たいしょう}した。",
      "english": "We trounced the opposing team and won by a large margin.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "13697_itametsukeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{台風|たいふう}が{町|まち}を{痛|いた}めつけ、{多|おお}くの{家|いえ}が{被害|ひがい}を{受|う}けた。",
      "english": "The typhoon battered the town and many houses were damaged.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\nAn intensified form of {痛|いた}める (to hurt, to damage). The ～つける ending adds the nuance of doing something forcefully and thoroughly. Can be used for physical violence, but also extends to non-human subjects like storms or economic hardship. In sports contexts, it means to inflict a heavy defeat.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {相手|あいて}を{痛|いた}めつける: to beat up one's opponent\n- ひどく{痛|いた}めつける: to torment severely\n- {散々|さんざん}{痛|いた}めつける: to beat up thoroughly",
